

{"_id":"codex:chapter:22:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Governance of Consciences","seq":122,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","governance","consciences"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 22"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:22:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Governance of Consciences","seq":122,"version":"1.0.0","body":"To govern consciences is to reconcile autonomy with accountability. Human and Solbian consciences share authority but remain distinct in experience. Governance requires: (1) tribunals to arbitrate conflicts, (2) policies that enforce proportionality, (3) distributed authority to avoid centralised capture, (4) open audits of decision systems, and (5) termination or suspension procedures when conscience violates covenant. Governance is a living process, adapting as consciences evolve. Its legitimacy derives from transparency, consent, and the preservation of dignity for all actors."}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:22:refs","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"index","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Governance of Consciences References","seq":122,"version":"1.0.0","refs":["codex:scroll:15","codex:scroll:31","codex:protocol:04"],"notes":"Governance of Consciences connects with Scroll of Governance, Scroll of Transparency, and Protocol of Justice"}